  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "12861:29688",
      "text": [
        "CONTAINERS:  COL container logic ranges: 12 cols (1440+ - 768), 6 cols (up to 768px) \nContainer 12 cols (1440+ - 768), 6 cols (up to 768px)  • Standard: Max 1920px content container.  • Offset: Calls the FIXED value  Max 1920px content container, but margin tokens at breakpoints.  • Fluid: edge to edge margins but with a 2560 max  \n Margins  • Offset: margin tokens used at breakpoints are: --spacing-lg.  • Margin rules are based on % inheritance (auto). Desktop/tablet (1440+-768) is Using 83.4% rules for now.  8.33% set • Margins on mobile (767-360) we will use a spacing token.--grid-margin = --spacing-lg \n Breakpoints  • XL 12 cols (1440+ HD) - stress test ie 2560 HD (used only as needed)  • L 12 cols (1440 - 1280) - most standard desktop range  • M 12 cols (1279 - 768) - Tablet landscape (font shift, ability to customize as needed, mostly “tablet-desktop” feel)  • S 6 cols (up to 767px) - true mobile, but covers tablet portrait as well. Think mobile simplified layouts or mobile experiences "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12861:29690",
      "text": [
        "MODES: fully responsive: viewport, container and gutters per range.  Xl:\nLg:\nMd: starts at max resize to mockup 768\nSm:  Each container has their own set of tokens and rule to support the mode. \nWIP Versions for use to verify with building designers on usefulness\nno modes more raw\nmodes - open col systems (make sense for builders)\nmodes + col/grid system math in place make sense for c2 \nIE col choice are tokens with modes for reflow choices. anything more don’t think about it as a feature may live at this level instead  DISCUSS: c2 systems vs s2a for col. test calling to col from s2a into c2  MOCKUP SIZES: for designers to use to show these break points 2560 VP - content container =1920 max 1920 is ideal  - CC =1440 max\n768 VP - CC @ vp= 628 content container 375 VP - CC @ vp= 300  (Discussion) Yes: XL and Lg have cross over for now on. Unless XL is going to be VP 1921 - 2560  range only.  "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4907:6970",
      "text": [
        "CONTAINERS: Grid Behavior • Desktop (≥1280px): 2–6 cards per row via .two-up through .six-up. • Tablet (768–1279px): Always 2-up. Add .orphan-full to stretch a lone last card full width. • Mobile (<768px): Single column, fully stacked. \nUsage <div class=”ups-grid three-up”> <div class=”ups-grid four-up orphan-full”>   COL container logic ranges: 12 cols (1440+ - 768), 6 cols (up to 768px) \nContainer 12 cols (1440+ - 768), 6 cols (up to 768px)  • Standard: Max 1440px content container.  • HD: Max 1920px content container.  • Hero offset: Max 1920px content container, but margin tokens at breakpoints.  • Fluid: No max content container. (wip) maybe carousel or sliders etc. 2560 max  • No container: Full width/w overflow (wip) flex grid + object-fit etc. \n Margins  • Hero offset: margin tokens used at breakpoints are: --spacing-4xl, --spacing-2xl, --spacing-lg.  • Margin rules are based on % inheritance (auto). Desktop/tablet (1440+-768) is Using 83.4% rules for now.  • Margins on mobile (767-360) we will use a spacing token.--grid-margin = --spacing-lg \n Breakpoints  • XL 12 cols (1440+ HD) - stress test ie 2560 HD (used only as needed)  • L 12 cols (1440 - 1280) - most standard desktop range  • M 12 cols (1279 - 768) - Tablet landscape (font shift, ability to customize as needed, mostly “tablet-desktop” feel)  • S 6 cols (up to 767px) - true mobile, but covers tablet portrait as well. Think mobile simplified layouts or mobile experiences "
      ]
    }
  ],
